77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T (Acne vulgaris is one of the most prevalent dermatological conditions worldwide, affecting a significant portion of the population in both adolescence and adulthood. Acne rates have been rising since the 1990s, with Western Europe identified as having the highest prevalence among world regions [1]. High-income, industrialised regions \(including Europe and North America\) report the greatest acne burden, likely due to lifestyle factors such as diet and urban environment [2]. The United States, for example, is estimated to have about 50 million people affected by acne at any given time.[2])
/E (Acne vulgaris is one of the most prevalent dermatological conditions worldwide, affecting a significant portion of the population in both adolescence and adulthood. Acne rates have been rising since the 1990s, with Western Europe identified as having the highest prevalence among world regions [1]. High-income, industrialised regions \(including Europe and North America\) report the greatest acne burden, likely due to lifestyle factors such as diet and urban environment [2]. The United States, for example, is estimated to have about 50 million people affected by acne at any given time.[2])
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
